## Initial design vision

Author request: "Ticket the initial design vision", following "Imagine 3 modes:
Fulltext, Structured-text, Chunks stream" and "Chunking strategy is a menu".
This records the direction for design work, not a finalized wire contract or
authorization to implement a semantic-search system.

Extend the existing full-text API plugin rather than invent another plugin
merely to expose text. Its current source is
bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin/bootstrap.js, with client bench/zotero_fulltext.py.
It already registers control/status endpoints on Zotero's local HTTP server;
it does not yet serve the structured-text views proposed here. A shipping
extension belongs under plugins/ per AGENTS.md; any promotion should preserve
its installation identity and lifecycle rather than create an unrelated add-on.

## Framing: a shared text foundation for Zotero AI tools

The sitter prepares structured text; the API plugin exposes it through a common
document-access contract. The intended convergence is on extraction reuse,
source locations, citation anchors, freshness and optional chunking strategies.
Consumers remain free to choose their models, embedding runtimes, indexes,
ranking methods and user interfaces.

This is a proposed shared foundation, not a claim of ecosystem adoption or
convergence of the whole AI stack. Adoption would need a stable documented
contract, simple installation and compatibility tests that independent tools
can run. Tools that must operate while Zotero is closed may also need an export
or snapshot path; that is a candidate follow-up, not part of the initial scope.
Keep the interface suitable for eventual native provision by Zotero, so the
plugins can yield to a platform capability without forcing consumer rewrites.

## The modes

| Mode | Intended representation | Typical use |
|---|---|---|
| Fulltext | Plain text in reading order | Reading, export, text processing |
| Structured-text | Blocks with types, flow classes, headings, page anchors and available positions | Citations, navigation, consumer-defined segmentation |
| Chunks stream | Successive passages with text, heading context and source locations, produced by a selected strategy | Incremental embedding and retrieval pipelines |

These are views of the same extraction, carrying a shared source and processor
identity. Fulltext describes a representation, not a requirement to allocate
or return a whole book at once. The bounded-read and identity contract remains
owned by SPEC.md through the existing contract work in 0726.

## Chunking strategy is a menu

The author specified that callers choose a strategy. Candidate entries from
the discussion, to evaluate rather than treat as a ratified release roster:

- Page: preserve individual page boundaries.
- Paragraph: preserve natural paragraph boundaries.
- Section: follow document headings and hierarchy.
- Token budget: bound passages against a specified tokenizer, with an overlap
  option where supported.
- #6012: reuse its section-aware splitting and merging policy at a pinned
  implementation version.

Each strategy exposes only meaningful parameters and states its guarantees.
A page or section may exceed an embedding model's input window; offering it
does not imply a token bound. Page locations accompany all strategies where
the extraction supplies them. Chunk responses identify the strategy, version
and effective parameters so consumers can invalidate downstream work when
boundaries change.

## Responsibility boundary

The sitter prepares native structured-text packs. The API provides access to
the available extraction and derived views. Embedding, GPU execution, vector
storage, ranking and MCP translation remain consumer concerns; this feature
does not require choosing any of them or resuming the held indexer rewrite.

The discussed read-path proposal is to return explicit missing/stale states
rather than silently wait for extraction. Final stale-read and preparation
semantics belong in the contract review, including whether a read can ever
request preparation explicitly. Turning the sitter off must not by itself
make already available text unreadable.

## Existing work and unresolved design

0726 owns the structured-text API contract; 0572 owns the Zoteus consumer.
This ticket supplies the initial product vision to that work, not a second
implementation train. Read those tickets and their logs before coding. The
remaining chunk-consumption and tokenizer-budget decisions are already recorded
under 0726 in DECISIONS.md; the strategy menu does not silently settle them.

Contract review should also settle:

- The first supported strategies, defaults, option validation and discovery.
- How extraction without physical pages represents locations.
- How callers resume bounded reads, and detect extraction replacement between
  requests without mixing document versions.
- Strategy state across response boundaries: transport pagination must not
  accidentally redefine paragraph, section or overlap geometry.
- Which version/identity information all modes share and what chunks add.
- Promotion of the existing measurement plugin to a maintained package, its
  compatibility with Zotero 10, and the fate of its existing control endpoints.

No numerical budget, API path or latency promise is chosen here.

## Exit criteria for this design ticket

- [ ] Review the initial vision against 0726, 0572, existing plugin code and
      SPEC.md's owning sections; record accepted scope and unresolved choices.
- [ ] Record any resulting rulings in DECISIONS.md first, then update SPEC.md
      and reconcile 0726 so requirements have one owner.
- [ ] Route concrete implementation and verification work through the existing
      owners, with machine-readable dependencies where sequencing is needed.
- [ ] Cover cross-mode text/location consistency, bounded/resumable reads,
      mid-stream identity changes, strategy semantics and cache-only availability
      in the resulting test plan; do not claim these tests already exist.
- [ ] make check passes for the resulting design change.
